on in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking and Giving Permission", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you ask for permission, it is important to be polite.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Can I please feed the animals now?</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter's Dad</span>: Of course, Peter!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You often use a modal like <span class=\"italic\">can, may, could</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to ask for permission.</p> You can also ask a Yes or No question like <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIs it OK if \u2026 \u201d</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\u201cDo you mind \u2026 \u201d</span></p> Here are some ways to ask for and give permission.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asking for Permission\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Giving Permission\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could I take a few days off next week?</p> Can I ask you something?</p> Would it be alright if I change projects?</p> Do you mind if someone takes my shifts next week?</p> Is it OK if I leave early today?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sure.</p> Perhaps.</p> Of course.</p> No problem.</p> I don't mind.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "distinctly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very clearly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I remember distinctly when I rode on a camel at the zoo.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a zoo visit.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to kid", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a joke or to say something and not mean it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I said you could feed the bear, but I was just kidding. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "camel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a tall four-legged animal with a long neck and two humps", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can take a ride on a camel at the zoo.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "zookeeper", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who looks after the animals at the zoo", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The zookeeper said I shouldn't feed the bears.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a big furry four-legged animal that is very strong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Bears like to eat salmon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cool", "type": "name"}, {"content": "interesting or good", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rhinos at the zoo look so cool.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go to the Franklin Park Zoo website.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find the map in English, and locate the 5<br>different animal areas. Write down the name and two animals from each area.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out what hours the zoo is opened on <br>weekends and the price of tickets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Organize your information in the table below. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 7 sentences with the information<br> from the table.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the information from your<br> sentences with your partner.<br><br><br><br><br><br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Zoo  Weekend Hours</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Ticket Prices</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adults: $\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Children: $\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Animal Area Name</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Animal #1</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \